    "id": "rule-k-g-pronunciation",
    "title": "German 'g' at the end of a word sounds like 'k'",
    "description": "Not a spelling correspondence with English, but a pronunciation rule worth knowing: German final 'g' is often devoiced to a 'k' sound (auslautverhärtung). Same word, different pronunciation depending on position — useful for reading words like Tag out loud.",
